From: Bonesaw
Subject: [PATCH] Worldserver image carries the modules sources, so module DB
 updaters stop crash-looping the container

apps/docker/Dockerfile -- one build file, not tracked in this repo (see
modules/mod-living-gear/core-patches/README.md for why and how to apply
this). Note this is under apps/, not src/server/, but it is the same
situation: vendored upstream AzerothCore that this repo does not track.

The Dockerfile copies `modules modules` into the db-import stage only. The
worldserver stage inherits from `runtime`, whose skeleton creates an empty
/azerothcore/modules and nothing ever fills it.

That is invisible until a module's own database updater is switched on.
`ENV AC_UPDATES_ENABLE_DATABASES=0` in the worldserver stage reads like it
covers this, but it only silences the CORE updater -- each module carries its
own switch, and mod-playerbots has `Playerbots.Updates.EnableDatabases` in
playerbots.conf. With that at 1 the worldserver resolves playerbots SQL
against /azerothcore/modules/mod-playerbots at runtime, does not find it, and
calls Shutting down. Combined with `restart: unless-stopped` in
docker-compose.yml that is a crash loop, not a single failure.

The nasty part is the delay between cause and symptom. A worldserver container
that is already running never re-reads any of this, so the realm can sit up for
weeks over a broken image. It only bites on the next `docker compose down` +
`up` -- which means it surfaces during whatever unrelated maintenance happened
to recreate the container and looks like that maintenance broke the realm. On
2026-09-01 it cost an outage during a disk-space cleanup, and three wrong
theories before anyone looked inside the image and found /azerothcore/modules
simply empty.

After applying, verify with:

    docker compose build ac-worldserver
    docker run --rm --entrypoint sh acore/ac-wotlk-worldserver:master \
        -c "ls -d /azerothcore/modules/mod-playerbots/data/sql/playerbots"

--- a/apps/docker/Dockerfile
+++ b/apps/docker/Dockerfile
@@ -188,9 +188,21 @@
 # This disables user prompts. The console is still active, however
 ENV AC_DISABLE_INTERACTIVE=1
 ENV AC_CLOSE_IDLE_CONNECTIONS=0

+# AC_UPDATES_ENABLE_DATABASES=0 above only silences the CORE updater. Module
+# updaters have their own switches -- playerbots.conf has
+# Playerbots.Updates.EnableDatabases -- and when one is on, worldserver resolves
+# its SQL against /azerothcore/modules at runtime. Without these sources the
+# image only has the empty dir made in the skeleton stage, so the updater aborts
+# with "the given source directory does not exist" and restart: unless-stopped
+# turns that into a crash loop. A long-running container hides it completely; it
+# only surfaces on the next `docker compose down` + `up`, which is how it cost an
+# outage during unrelated disk maintenance on 2026-09-01.
+COPY --chown=$DOCKER_USER:$DOCKER_USER \
+    modules modules
+
 COPY --chown=$DOCKER_USER:$DOCKER_USER \
      --from=build \
      /azerothcore/env/dist/bin/worldserver /azerothcore/env/dist/bin/worldserver

 VOLUME /azerothcore/env/dist/etc
